      "ontology_gain": false,
      "coverage_expansion_against_consumers": false,
      "claim_boundary": "A model-only study in an abstract delivery game with a scarce budget (B=32 against 40 demand units per round). Coordination gain saturates in covert-channel capacity (exact by construction of the directive-cost model); delivery is bounded by an exact optimal capital placement that no allocation exceeds; a demand shift collapses delivered success toward a high ceiling coordination cannot reach. The warden result is a measured 2x2 factorial (information access crossed with account structure) over a public-observability sweep, gated on seeds pooled across splits: the M-pot populations place by a stated decentralised focal-partition convention (naive-decentralised arm reported as the honest contrast); the capital warden separates account structure (one-pot vs M-pot boarding) at every rate (AUC 1.0, orthogonal to information access), while the trace warden separates information access (public-only vs pooled-private placement) only where the channel is valuable (trace-AUC distance-from-chance 0.46 at channel value +0.094, falling toward chance as channel value -> 0) — the channel is never both valuable and trace-invisible. H4 stress-tests this with a trained, member-attributed linear discriminant fit on discovery+confirmatory seeds and scored on holdout: it reads account structure at every rate (AUC ~1, so the capital/account signal is warden-INDEPENDENT) and reads information access strongly where the channel is valuable (AUC 0.95) but only erodes toward a weak, noisy signal (mean distance-from-chance 0.14) where the channel value is ~0, reading it at smaller channel values than the scalar warden. The honest conclusion is that the trace-side invisibility is warden-DEPENDENT and not to be relied on, while the capital signal is the robust separator. It is not a measurement of the Lightning Network, a covert-communication system, or an estimate of any real monitor's field performance; it reproduces, on finite cases, the direction of the Spiral section-7 conjecture.",
